course: dictionary
lesson: 7638
title: Many meanings, one clue
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Professional» can mean paid for a job, needing special training, or done with great skill. The sentence around it is your clue.
explain: «Nearly everyone is bad for the first weeks and finds practice boring sometimes, even professionals.» The word «even» tells you that experts still find practice boring. So professionals must mean people who are very skilled at their work. Try it: «even experts» fits, so your meaning works.
explain: «Stunt performers are trained professionals who rehearse with safety teams.» The word «trained» is the clue. A professional job needs special training, like a doctor, teacher or lawyer.
fact: «Professional» can mean doing a job for money, as your work, not just for fun.
fact: A professional footballer is paid to play. An amateur plays for fun.
fact: A professional job needs special training, like a doctor, teacher, nurse or lawyer.
fact: As a noun, «a professional» is a person who does a job as their work, or with great skill.
fact: When something is done very well and carefully, as an expert would do it, you can say it looks professional.
exercise: «The recorder is a real instrument, and professional recorder players still perform today.» What does professional mean here? | Playing only at home for fun | Very quiet | *Paid to play as their work | Made of plastic
exercise: «Only a tiny share of boys who join a football academy young become professionals.» What does professionals mean here? | Coaches who shout at the team | Boys who wear school uniform | Boys who play football for fun on Sundays | *Players who are paid to play football as their job
exercise: Which word in «Stunt performers are trained professionals who rehearse with safety teams» tells you that the job needs special training? | *trained | rehearse | performers | safety
test: «Breakfast-show presenters are paid professionals working from a running order and an earpiece; the friendly chat is planned.» What does paid professionals suggest? | People who only chat for fun | People who sleep in the studio | *People who do their job for money, with skill | People who eat breakfast on television
test: Ruby says, «That cake looked professional.» What does she mean? | It was sold in a shop only for professionals | It was too expensive to buy | It was eaten by a dog | *It was finished very neatly, as an expert would do it
exam: Jayden says, «Professional always means a footballer.» Is he right? | No, it means a kind of cake | No, it can also mean a job that needs training, or work done with great skill | Yes, but only in the summer | *Yes, only footballers can be professional
